133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Mounting the cells securely is crucial to the entire system. A cell coming loose can lead to catastrophic failure. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Furthermore, mechanical and electrical integrity go hand in hand while designing cell housings. A bad mechanical design can lead to sub-optimal electrical results.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The cell housing also needs to be insulating and fire resistant while being able to conduct electricity through the electrical connections.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Modularity is also crucial for making changes easily as our designs will require a lot of iteration under a tight budget.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
